# Code reuse (DRY)

When you **add or change** code under `gdtracker/` or `gdtracker-api/`:

## Trigger

If **non-trivial logic** (validation, mapping, formatting, parsing, repeated HTTP/error handling, repeated UI structure) **already exists elsewhere**, or you are **copying** an existing pattern—**stop and consolidate** instead of duplicating.

## Where to put shared code

**Backend (`gdtracker-api/`)**

- **`.../util/`** — stateless helpers (formatting, dates, pure functions). Prefer `final` classes with private constructors for static-only helpers.
- **`service/`** — domain or business rules used by multiple callers (`@Service`).
- **`dto/` / mapping** — repeated request/response shaping; keep mapping near DTOs or a dedicated mapper if the project adds one.

Avoid a catch-all “utils” dumping ground for domain rules; put domain logic in services.

**Frontend (`gdtracker/`)**

- **`src/util/`** — pure TS helpers.
- **`src/api/`** — HTTP clients and API-shaped helpers (axios usage).
- **`components/`** — repeated UI; extract shared pieces when duplication is real.
- **Custom hooks** — repeated state/effects (e.g. under `src/hooks/` or colocated where the repo already places hooks).

## Exceptions

One-off glue, generated code, or extraction that would **couple unrelated modules**—note briefly (commit/PR/chat) why duplication stays.

## Documentation

When you add a **new reusable module** or a **meaningful helper surface**, update that project’s **Shared utilities & reuse** section in `docs/` in the **same** change when feasible (see `docs/OVERVIEW.md` / `docs/README.md`).
